---
description: WorkHarness architecture and coding rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Read and follow `AGENTS.md` before planning or editing. WorkHarness is a
Run-centric local AI Agent Harness, not a chat application.

- For work affecting agent context, prompts, provider requests, tools, MCP/ACP,
  retrieval, memory, history, compaction, subagents, or token/cost budgets,
  read and apply
  `.cursor/skills/workharness-context-engineering/SKILL.md` together with
  `AGENTS.md`, then include its context-impact note in the final report.
- Preserve `View -> ViewModel -> Service -> HarnessEngine` dependency flow.
- Keep providers and real tools behind MCP boundaries.
- Keep full coding agents behind `AgentRuntime`, preferably ACP.
- Use the existing Screen/Page/View/ViewModel/Design structure.
- Append important actions as immutable `RunEvent` values.
- Keep bug fixes minimal and add deterministic focused tests.
- Run the macOS build and relevant tests after Swift changes.
- Never commit or push without an explicit request.

Use `CLAUDE.md` for concrete project examples, anti-patterns, and the typical
Swift file template.
